# Why this Module ships no seed/ directory.
# A marker with no justification is a silent skip in file form; lint-config
# refuses an empty one.

The buckets are provisioned by the minio-init helper, not by a seed directory.
Its `command:` reads MINIO_BUCKETS, runs `mc mb --ignore-existing` and `mc
version enable` for each name, then exits 0. That is where new buckets are added
— editing MINIO_BUCKETS in .env.example, not dropping files here. Object content
itself is runtime data written through the S3 API.
